{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00358",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 5.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Uh, good evening, doctor, thank you for staying late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.87,
      "end_seconds": 9.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "You're fine, sit down. So, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 11.33,
      "end_seconds": 15.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "Doctor, I'm just here to help with the details."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.82,
      "end_seconds": 23.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Of course, please stay. It's helpful to have you here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.26,
      "end_seconds": 36.39,
      "duration_seconds": 12.13,
      "text": "Yeah, it's a red eye. I don't know what's causing it. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.0,
      "end_seconds": 39.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.58,
      "end_seconds": 43.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "It's, It's been about four days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.32,
      "end_seconds": 56.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.7,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps. I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.54,
      "end_seconds": 77.34,
      "duration_seconds": 20.8,
      "text": "Only a cold compress, and it's not much. Pretty moderate, if I'm being honest. My family kept telling me to get it checked. Oh, and watering. That's been about the same, five days. And there's a sticky discharge in the morning as well, uh, about two weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.21,
      "end_seconds": 82.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Any contact lens, cold, sensitivity to light or pain in the eye?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.01,
      "end_seconds": 84.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.47,
      "end_seconds": 87.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Has there been any loss of vision?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.55,
      "end_seconds": 90.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "No, no loss of vision."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.75,
      "end_seconds": 93.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.46,
      "end_seconds": 97.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "No, you know, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 98.62,
      "end_seconds": 106.82,
      "duration_seconds": 8.2,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Respiratory rate 18, pulse is 69 beats a minute, blood pressure 113 over 81."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.46,
      "end_seconds": 111.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "Alright, thanks. Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.86,
      "end_seconds": 134.15,
      "duration_seconds": 22.29,
      "text": "I have eczema, for about ten years. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. High cholesterol, for about a year. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't. Uh, I've had asthma, yes. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.25,
      "end_seconds": 147.3,
      "duration_seconds": 12.05,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known eczema. We'll keep that in mind today. Right, so that's your known high cholesterol. We'll keep that in mind today. So, what about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.35,
      "end_seconds": 154.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.75,
      "text": "My mother had high blood pressure. My father had a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.57,
      "end_seconds": 156.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.02,
      "end_seconds": 164.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "Yes, aspirin. I get a rash. I'm allergic to sulfa drugs, I get a rash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.0,
      "end_seconds": 167.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.79,
      "end_seconds": 176.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Hydrocortisone cream. I take it when needed. I take rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 177.44,
      "end_seconds": 187.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.64,
      "text": "Okay, so doctor, I think the last prescription for the rosuvastatin was 20 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.25,
      "end_seconds": 191.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.5,
      "end_seconds": 198.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "No, I left it at home. Asthalin inhaler. I take it when needed for my asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.99,
      "end_seconds": 201.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Right, any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.41,
      "end_seconds": 203.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.51,
      "text": "No operations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.63,
      "end_seconds": 209.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.16,
      "end_seconds": 210.86,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.62,
      "end_seconds": 214.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "Now bend it for me, slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.36,
      "end_seconds": 239.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "The white of the eye is pink all over, and there's some sticky discharge on the lashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.23,
      "end_seconds": 241.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.32,
      "end_seconds": 245.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.91,
      "end_seconds": 261.03,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Your vision is normal on the chart and the pupil reacts well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.13,
      "end_seconds": 262.83,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.61,
      "end_seconds": 279.9,
      "duration_seconds": 11.29,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with conjunctivitis. I can't rule out an allergic eye problem yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.99,
      "end_seconds": 284.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "I mean, is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.43,
      "end_seconds": 298.79,
      "duration_seconds": 13.36,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like conjunctivitis, but I'd like to confirm. Let's get an eye swab, for red eye. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.09,
      "end_seconds": 301.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.71,
      "end_seconds": 329.12,
      "duration_seconds": 26.41,
      "text": "Let's use chloramphenicol eye drops, four times a day, for five days. That's for conjunctivitis. Wash your hands often, don't share towels, and don't rub the eye. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.7,
      "end_seconds": 332.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.22,
      "end_seconds": 342.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "If your vision drops or the pain gets severe, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.44,
      "end_seconds": 345.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Okay, uh, I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.57,
      "end_seconds": 351.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Please come and see me if it's not better in three days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.33,
      "end_seconds": 356.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Um, sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 357.39,
      "end_seconds": 360.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.36,
      "end_seconds": 365.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "No, um, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}